@* Copyable XGID badge, rendered in normal flow wherever the host places it.
   The visible text is clipped to the value's own "XGID=" prefix (app.css), so it
   reads as the label for the icon-only copy button beside it; the full value
   goes to the clipboard, to the tooltip, to a select-all, and to a screen
   reader. Renders nothing when the XGID is empty (see the code-behind). *@
@if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Xgid))
{
    <div class="xgid-label" role="group" aria-label="Position XGID">
        @* title, because the visible text is clipped to a cap the board's size
           depends on — the full value stays in the DOM, on the clipboard, and
           in a select-all. *@
        <code class="xgid-label-text" title="@Xgid">@Xgid</code>
        @* Icon-only, and its accessible name is real text rather than an
           aria-label: the same span carries the copy's result — copied, or
           refused — so a screen-reader user is told what happened instead of
           watching a glyph they cannot see change. *@
        <button type="button"
                class="xgid-label-copy @_copy.ShowingClass"
                title="@Name"
                @onclick="CopyAsync">
            <span class="visually-hidden">@Name</span>
        </button>
    </div>
}
